#### 7. 'wiggle' (unweighted) is oriented for the drawn order; only 'weighted_wiggle' is reversed
ok   m3 example (3 layers x 7): 'wiggle' == drawn-order midline minimiser -(1/m) sum (m - i - 1/2) f_i
ok   m3 example (3 layers x 7): 'wiggle' differs from the reversed-order midline minimiser -(1/m) sum (i + 1/2) f_i
ok   m3 example (3 layers x 7): integrating the unit-weight per-step minimiser reproduces the 'wiggle' closed form (up to its constant)
ok   4 layers x 5: 'wiggle' == drawn-order midline minimiser -(1/m) sum (m - i - 1/2) f_i
ok   4 layers x 5: 'wiggle' differs from the reversed-order midline minimiser -(1/m) sum (i + 1/2) f_i
ok   4 layers x 5: integrating the unit-weight per-step minimiser reproduces the 'wiggle' closed form (up to its constant)
